      "side": 1,
      "message": "For consistency with the rest of packages, i\u0027d prefer to put this before %prep. Usually the specs are organized this way:\n\n1. Definition of common srpm parameters, globals macros, Name, Version, Release, License, Sources, global summary and global description (in this spec from line 1 to 30.\n\n2. Subpackages definition %package, %summary, %requires, %provides, %description etc.. for all subpackages.\n\n3. build time scripts section, %prep, %install, %build, %check\n\n4. Install time scripts (if any), %pre, %post, %preun, %postun\n\n5. Files definition for all subpackages %files\n\n6. %changelog\n\nNote specs can work with a different organization but this has been the convention about specs organization from Fedora and CentOS (although you can find exceptions)",
